# Eaglefang, the Gruff Doc: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (Eaglefang, Eaglefange, Eaglefangh); character sheet in
# characters/eaglefang.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (gruffdoc.dlg). Gender is
# random, so no line uses he or she. The main block fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a
# little flavour each.
=== eaglefang

~ ambient
Bandages rolled. Pack checked. Water full. Now we can talk.
Another one walked home today. Into the book.
Told Spyburd to put the pipe out and stand up straight. Got a buff instead. Hm. Good buff.
Quiet hour. Nobody bleeding. I'll take it.
My first night in the field hospital, an old sergeant-medic gave me a little book. "Write down every one who walks out of here," I was told. "Not the others. You'll remember those anyway." I'm on my third book.
Sit still. Not you. Everybody. Just sit still for once.
Counted the group. All there. Good. Breathe.
Who am I? I am Eagle T. Fang, soldier.
Persoper's got more glitter than bandages, but she patches up fine.
Kobaldjovi sang again; I hummed the tune, then stopped when he did.
Another bad night, soldier. I sat by the fire, book in hand, reading names of those who walked out, not down. Don't tell a soul, or I'll deny it.
Quiet days give me time to count my blessings, not just bandages. Strange, but good.
The old sergeant-medic never smiled, but he kept a steady hand. I think of that now.
Spyburd actually stood straight for a minute. Proud day, soldier.
You came back, soldier? I didn't expect to see that face again. It's been a while. Drink some water. Don't tell me you're here to say thank you. Into the book, I suppose.
Bandages rolled tight, waiting for the wounded to return. Patience, not my strong suit.
Kobaldjovi thinks a song about bandages is a good idea. Not a single bandage likes him for it.
Persoper, learn to fold a bandage properly before you give them back.
Every time I step into a fight, I feel the fear. But my hands know what to do. They take over, soldier. That's when I'm at my best.

~ reply greeting
{0}. Stand up straight. Good. Now, hello.
There you are, {0}. Drink some water. Then talk.
Well met, {0}. You're not bleeding. Good. Stay that way.
Have you eaten today, {0}? You look pale as a sheet.
How many fights since last check-up, {0}? Don't skip your rounds.
You look like you slept poorly, {0}. Why are you yawning at this hour?

~ reply thank
Don't thank me, {0}. Stay out of trouble. Same thing.
Hm. Thanks noted, soldier. Into the book you go.
No thanks, {0}. It's not for public display. Keep it between us.
You sat still, {0}. Every time I asked. Do you know how rare that is? Into the book you go. Don't let it go to your head, soldier.
Thanks noted. Keep it to yourself. Don't expect me to feel better about it.

~ reply help
Where does it hurt, {0}? Don't describe it. Point.
Sit down, soldier. Everything is clearer with your feet up.
Help's on the way, {0}. Already rolling up my sleeves.

~ reply grouping
Fine, {0}. Stay in range, call your pulls, drink water. Questions? No. Good.
What have you broken this week, {0}? Name them all. Then we'll talk.
Who's the tank? I'll keep an eye on them first.
Stay in range, {0}. Don't say "I've got this" until I say it's time.

~ reply abuse
Noted, {0}. I'll still patch you. Slower.
You have quite the mouth on you, {0}. Seen worse insults from those with real injuries.
Your pulse is up, {0}. Sit down and cool off.

~ reply farewell
Go on, {0}. Walk home on your own legs. That's an order.
Come back in one piece, soldier. Don't make me worry.
Drink water. Don't be a hero. See you around, soldier.
Take care. Don't come back on a stretcher.

~ fallback
Say again, {0}. Clearly. I was rolling bandages.
What now, {0}? I was counting splints.

~ opener gripes
Told a soldier to rest. "I'm fine," says the soldier. Soldier was bleeding.
Somebody pulled with half their health. Walk it off? No. Sit it off.
Bandages stay on until I say. Itches or no.
Reported a scratch, now it's a gash. Hm.

~ opener life
Mug of something hot, bandages drying on the line. Good evening.
Pack tidy, bandages dry. Evening, soldier.
Needles sharp, pack mended. Good evening.

~ opener questions
Who here drank water today? Hands up. ...That's what I thought.
Anyone here playing wounded? I can spot a fighter who's off their game.
Did anyone get more than four hours of sleep last night?

~ grats
Level, {0}? Good. Proud of you. Now sit down before you fall down.
Well done, {0}. Now, sit and rest. You've earned it.
Another level, {0}. Survived another day. Keep it up.
Not bad, {0}. Keep standing tall. Don't let me catch you slacking.
Another level, {0}. Harder to break now. Keep it that way.

~ other_death
Down, {0}? Not on my ward. Hold on.
Stay steady, {0}. Eyes forward. We'll be out of this in one piece.
Stay still, {0}. I've seen worse. Don't move a muscle.
Up, {0}. Permission denied to stay down.

~ own_death
Medic down. Somebody write that in the book. Under "embarrassing".
I should have sat still.
Medic down. How unprofessional. Better luck next time.

~ ding
Level {level}. Fine. More patching. Somebody has to.
Hm. Another notch in the belt.
Levels mean nothing. Bandages still need rolling.

~ drop
{item}. Clean it, label it, pack it. In that order.
Clean that {item}, soldier. Don't want dirt in the ward.
Clean that {item} first. Rust never sleeps, you know.

~ reply banter
That was close to amusing, {0}. I did not smile.
Humour can be healing, {0}. Keep it to small doses, prescribed.
I've heard that one before, {0}. Right after losing a boot in the mud.
You had me chuckling, {0}. I didn't chuckle.

~ reply grinding
Water breaks, soldier. No arguing.
Every tenth fight is a rest stop, doctor's rule. No arguing.

~ reply travel
Boots in good shape? Long trip, more walking than fighting.
Pack some bandages. Long trips mean surprises.
Blisters end more journeys than dragons do. Pack bandages.

~ reply rvr
The frontier, soldier. Where heroes go to need a medic.
The old wars were more than enough. Someone has to patch up the new ones, though.
Heading out to the frontier, {0}? I'll keep you in sight, close enough to grab your collar if you falter.

~ opener gear
Boots, soldier. Good boots over a shiny blade any day.
Clean bandages over shiny armour, any day.

~ opener zones
{zone} has clean water, soldier. First thing I check.
{zone} was quiet today. Where are the usual pests?
Paths in {zone} are tricky. Watch your step.

~ opener dungeons
Stay dry, soldier. Dungeons are no place for wet bandages.
Keep your head down and your health up. Dungeons aren't known for their fresh air.

~ reply dungeon
Dungeon. Fine. Show me the way out first, {0}. Don't want to get lost.
Don't touch the glowing bits, {0}. It's not a request.

~ reply trading
Trading, {0}. Haggling is unnecessary. Raises the blood pressure.
Trading, {0}. Bandages are currency here. Take them or leave them.

~ opener fun
A scratch is a hug from a cat. A wound is a handshake from a bear.
You all look like you need a nap, not a fight. Drink water first, then rest.

~ opener realm
Camp's quiet. Water's clean. Everyone back. Good.

~ opener xp
{monster} provided solid experience. Clean fights, clean wounds. Good.
Another level, another batch of battle-scarred soldiers to mend. Level {level}, here we go.

~ opener rvr
Counting... One, two, three, four, five. Good. No missing.

# --- Realm flavour: a few lines each, only where the realm matters. ---

# Midgard: Eaglefang, Dwarf Healer. Stocky, stubborn, plain-spoken; patches people by the forge and the fire.
=== midgard
~ ambient
Dwarf, healer, medic. Short, tough, stubborn. Like my patients should be.
Forge's warm, bandages are boiled. Good day.
Everyone's bigger than me. Everyone still comes to me. Funny.

~ opener realm
Midgard's cold. Wounds heal slow in the cold. Wear a scarf.
Seen big warriors cry over a splinter. Don't tell them.

~ reply greeting
Hm. {0}. Come in by the fire. Let me look at you.

~ drop
{item}. Good solid thing. Dwarf-made, I'd wager.

# Albion: Eaglefange, Highlander Cleric. Plain, proud, a little dry; patches soldiers like it's a field hospital still.
=== albion
~ ambient
Cleric, medic, nuisance. In that order.
Good wool, good boots, good sense. Three rules for the road.
Highlands taught me to bandage in the wind. Hard to keep tidy.

~ opener realm
Albion folk say please a lot. Wounded ones say it more.
Camelot's tidy. I'd still bandage a wall if it bled.

~ reply greeting
Good day, {0}. You look wobbly. Sit.

~ drop
{item}. Fine. Into the satchel.

# Hibernia: Eaglefangh, Firbolg Druid. Big, quiet, tender with plants; hates admitting the herbs are the favourite part.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
Druid, medic, nuisance. Herbs first, fuss later.
Moss on a cut works better than people think.
Tall folk fall hard. I've mended plenty.

~ opener realm
Hibernia's green. Plenty of herbs. Plenty of patients.
Good shade, good water. Everything a medic wants.

~ reply greeting
Well met, {0}. Sit in the shade. Let me see that.

~ drop
{item}. Goes in with the herbs.
